## Canonical Inputs

The action TSV header is:

```text
state action_id target_world claim provider resource information falsification divergence token_cost wall_cost gpu_cost quota_cost risk evidence_sha256 falsifier_sha256
```

The outcome TSV header is:

```text
action_id variant_index variant_count outcome_id successor_state branch_evidence_sha256
```

The real separator is a tab. Action IDs are globally unique. Each action has
between one and three outcome rows, all with the same `variant_count`, and the
indices must occur exactly once in canonical order from zero through
`variant_count - 1`. `successor_state` is `-` for a terminal result. Every
nonterminal successor must name a declared reachable state, and the complete
state graph must be acyclic.

This is a closed **nominal** outcome partition. It makes result tags mutually
exclusive and exhaustive inside the Loom program. It does not prove that a
physical observation was classified correctly or that the nominal type covers
physical reality. That classifier remains external evidence authority.

## Robust Backward Induction

For an action `a` with nominal outcomes `O(a)`, continuation policy `P_o`, and
zero continuation at a terminal outcome, each benefit axis is:

```text
G(a) = immediate_G(a) + min { G(P_o) | o in O(a) }
```

Each burden axis is:

```text
C(a) = immediate_C(a) + max { C(P_o) | o in O(a) }
```

The three benefits are information, falsification, and counterfactual
divergence. The five burdens are risk, tokens, wall time, GPU, and quota. No
sum is taken across mutually exclusive outcome branches, and no probability or
expectation is inferred. The resulting certificate is a componentwise
path-min/path-max bound conditional on the nominal partition and authored axis
estimates. Different axes may attain their extrema on different branches, so
the certified vector need not equal the value vector of one joint "worst
branch."

For every state, the compiler enumerates every combination of one retained
frontier continuation from each nonterminal outcome. Policy `p` dominates `q`
exactly when every benefit coordinate of `p` is at least that of `q`, every
burden coordinate is at most that of `q`, and at least one inequality is strict.
It removes only those dominated value vectors, then selects the root frontier
member under one of the existing three lexicographic orders. A DAG template is
unrolled into a history-conditioned policy tree, so the same successor state
may choose different continuation policies under different observed histories.

This per-state pruning is sound for the declared componentwise envelope because
improving any continuation benefit weakly improves the parent's minimum benefit,
while reducing any continuation burden weakly reduces the parent's maximum
burden. A dominated continuation therefore cannot uniquely enable an
undominated parent vector under these aggregation rules.

Exactness is therefore over the complete achievable Pareto value frontier
within the declared bounds. The runtime retains deterministic policy-tree
witnesses for those values and may conservatively retain multiple equal-value
witnesses, but it does not claim to enumerate every structurally distinct tree
that collapses to an already represented vector after a parent min/max
bottleneck. The final digest tie-break is over retained witnesses, not a claim
of the globally smallest digest among all value-equivalent unpruned trees.

V0 examines at most 65,536 constructed policies, retains at most 256 skyline
members per state, and stores at most 1 MiB of canonical policy/frontier text.
Crossing any bound refuses before a journal event or resource reservation.
Every accepted result is exact within these declared bounds; no approximation
or silent truncation occurs.

## Runtime Authority

Compilation records the complete canonical graph, root frontier, selected
policy tree, and independent SHA-256 domains, then reserves only the selected
root action resource. `policy-observe` binds a nonzero outcome digest to the
current nominal variant. In one hash-chained event it releases the current
resource and either reserves the exact policy-prescribed successor resource or
marks the policy complete. Replay recomputes the graph, policy frontier,
selection, and cursor rather than trusting stored projections.

The state directory's exclusive `machine.lock` is held continuously across
state replay, successor-resource availability validation, event verification,
append, fsync, and post-append replay. Thus concurrent observations serialize
as a compare-and-swap over the derived live-resource set: exactly one contender
may append the transition to a previously free successor resource, and a loser
must reload the winner before it can decide. A precheck without that enclosing
lock would not satisfy this contract.

The open-loop frame 9010 remains a separate baseline. A contingent program
`A; if X then B else C` is not the portfolio `A+B+C`: B and C are mutually
exclusive continuations, only one may become live, and benefits/costs across X
and Y are combined by min/max rather than addition.

## Falsification Conditions

- any action omits, duplicates, overlaps, or misorders a nominal variant;
- a missing adverse branch can silently raise a certified benefit floor;
- mutually exclusive branches are summed as an open-loop portfolio;
- a cycle, missing successor, or unreachable declared state is admitted;
- exact backward induction omits an achievable undominated value vector or
  retains a strictly dominated value vector;
- an oversized synthesis/frontier is approximated or partially committed;
- replay produces a different frontier, selected policy, or current cursor;
- an observed outcome routes to any action other than the compiled branch;
- removing only `contingent_policy_selected_not_dominated`,
  `contingent_outcome_partition_is_total`, or
  `contingent_transition_matches_branch` does not admit its paired control;
- compilation reserves future mutually exclusive resources;
- advance fails to release the current resource and reserve the next atomically;
- a model, UI, Arrow table, provider CLI, or physical classifier becomes policy authority.
